{
  "_comment": [
    "Noise-aware regression gate for eval_flagship.yml (src/gaia/eval/regression_gate.py).",
    "ONE source of truth for its thresholds and its quarantine; the workflow passes",
    "this file and nothing else.",
    "",
    "confirm_reruns: a scenario that went PASS->FAIL against the baseline is re-run",
    "up to this many times on the same machine, stopping at the first pass; it is a",
    "regression only if every re-run fails too. 2, not 1: replaying the runs below",
    "against the baseline (37110051697), each re-run passing at the scenario's",
    "measured rate, one re-run left about",
    "24% of runs red with no regression behind them and two left about 5%. The",
    "`confirm_reruns` dispatch input overrides it for one run.",
    "max_reruns_per_category: past this many flips in one category the rest are",
    "counted as confirmed without a re-run - no measured run had more than 2 outside",
    "the quarantine - and it keeps a lane's worst case (3 categories x 4 flips x 2",
    "re-runs at the slowest 6.7 min) inside the eval step's 360-min budget.",
    "category_max_confirmed_losses (K): a category fails at K confirmed regressions.",
    "category_max_pass_rate_drop_pp (P): a category also fails when its pass rate over",
    "the gated scenarios drops by more than P points, re-runs applied. With 6 or",
    "fewer gated scenarios, one confirmed regression is already more than 15 points.",
    "aggregate_max_lost_passes: the whole run fails when its judged passes over the",
    "scenarios both sides judged fall more than this below the baseline's.",
    "",
    "quarantine: scenarios measured as unstable. They still run and are reported as a",
    "::warning:: with the rate below, but never gate. Every entry needs a measured",
    "pass_rate, the number of judged runs it was measured over, and a tracking issue;",
    "tests/unit/eval/test_regression_gate.py fails on an entry without them. Remove an",
    "entry once the scenario is stable again (above 80% over 5+ runs), with the runs",
    "that show it.",
    "",
    "The initial list is every scenario that passed 20-80% of its judged runs (5+",
    "runs) across the 11 nightlies/dispatches on main with scorecards, 2026-09-30 to",
    "2026-10-11 (agent Gemma-4-E4B-it-GGUF, EVAL_MODEL claude-sonnet-4-6), plus",
    "baseline passes that failed more than 80% of those runs. main moved between",
    "those runs, so a rate mixes run-to-run noise with code changes."
  ],
  "confirm_reruns": 2,
  "max_reruns_per_category": 4,
  "category_max_confirmed_losses": 2,
  "category_max_pass_rate_drop_pp": 15,
  "aggregate_max_lost_passes": 0,
